2:T818,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average cost of a loft conversion in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a UK loft conversion may typically cost around £30,000–£100,000 or more. Roof light conversions can be less expensive than dormer, hip-to-gable or mansard designs, but every property and specification is different. Request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is a loft conversion cheaper than an extension?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It can be, because a loft conversion uses existing space and may avoid new foundations. However, major structural work, a new staircase, a bathroom or a large dormer can make the cost substantial. The best option depends on the available roof space and your needs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need planning permission for a loft conversion?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Some loft conversions may fall under permitted development, while others require planning permission. The answer depends on the design, property and local restrictions. Building regulations approval is a separate matter and should also be considered."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a dormer loft conversion cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a broad UK guide, a rear dormer conversion may typically cost around £45,000–£75,000. Structural changes, an en-suite, premium finishes, difficult access and combining the dormer with a hip-to-gable conversion can increase the price. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What should be included in a loft conversion quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Look for design and structural work, approvals, scaffolding, insulation, windows, electrics, plumbing, plastering, decorating, flooring, waste removal and final making good. Check exclusions and allowances so quotes can be compared fairly."}}]}7:["slug","how-much-does-a-loft-conversion-cost-uk","d"]
9:T4d5,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"HomeAndConstructionBusiness","name":"BMB Renovation","url":"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk","logo":"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/favicon.svg","image":"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/og-image.png","description":"BMB Renovation offers premium home, kitchen & bathroom renovation services in Watford, London & Hertfordshire. 15+ years of experience. Free consultation.","telephone":"+447775758717","email":"contact@bmbrenovation.co.uk","priceRange":"££","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"157 Judge Street","addressLocality":"Watford","postalCode":"WD24 5AN","addressRegion":"Hertfordshire","addressCountry":"GB"},"geo":{"@type":"GeoCoordinates","latitude":51.6549,"longitude":-0.3978},"areaServed":["Watford","Bushey","Rickmansworth","St Albans","Hemel Hempstead","Borehamwood","Harrow","Croxley Green","Luton","Bedford","London"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"},{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":"Saturday","opens":"09:00","closes":"16:00"}],"sameAs":["https://www.facebook.com/bmbrenovation","https://www.instagram.com/bmbrenovation"]}0:["1e5iN4Be4Hc13NMn4lWQ0",[[["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","how-much-does-a-loft-conversion-cost-uk","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__?{\"slug\":\"how-much-does-a-loft-conversion-cost-uk\"}",{}]}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",{"children":["blog",{"children":[["slug","how-much-does-a-loft-conversion-cost-uk","d"],{"children":["__PAGE__",{},[["$L1",["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen flex flex-col","children":[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"How Much Does a Loft Conversion Cost UK?\",\"description\":\"How much does a loft conversion cost UK? Compare typical prices by type and learn how planning, structure, finishes and extras affect your quote.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-07-30T10:29:10.917Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-07-30T10:29:10.917Z\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BMB Renovation\",\"url\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BMB Renovation\",\"url\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/og-image.png\"}},\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/blog/how-much-does-a-loft-conversion-cost-uk\",\"keywords\":\"loft conversion cost UK, loft conversion prices, dormer loft conversion cost, roof light conversion cost, loft conversion quote\"}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Blog\",\"item\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"How Much Does a Loft Conversion Cost UK?\",\"item\":\"https://bmbrenovation.co.uk/blog/how-much-does-a-loft-conversion-cost-uk\"}]}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$2"}}],["$","$L3",null,{}],["$","section",null,{"className":"relative pt-28 pb-12 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6","children":[["$","nav",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-white/50 mb-6","aria-label":"Breadcrumb","children":[["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/","className":"hover:text-[#C8A97E] transition-colors inline-flex items-center gap-1","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-house w-3.5 h-3.5","children":[["$","path","5wwlr5",{"d":"M15 21v-8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v8"}],["$","path","1d0kgt",{"d":"M3 10a2 2 0 0 1 .709-1.528l7-5.999a2 2 0 0 1 2.582 0l7 5.999A2 2 0 0 1 21 10v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"}],"$undefined"]}]," Home"]}],["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-3 h-3","children":[["$","path","mthhwq",{"d":"m9 18 6-6-6-6"}],"$undefined"]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"hover:text-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"Blog"}],["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-3 h-3","children":[["$","path","mthhwq",{"d":"m9 18 6-6-6-6"}],"$undefined"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white/80 truncate max-w-[200px] sm:max-w-none","children":"How Much Does a Loft Conversion Cost UK?"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-white/10 border border-white/10 text-[#C8A97E] text-xs mb-4","children":"how much does a loft conversion cost uk"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight leading-tight","children":"How Much Does a Loft Conversion Cost UK?"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 text-white/50 text-sm mt-5","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-calendar w-4 h-4","children":[["$","path","1cmpym",{"d":"M8 2v4"}],["$","path","4m81vk",{"d":"M16 2v4"}],["$","rect","1hopcy",{"width":"18","height":"18","x":"3","y":"4","rx":"2"}],["$","path","8toen8",{"d":"M3 10h18"}],"$undefined"]}],"30 July 2026",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-white/25","children":"·"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"BMB Renovation"}]]}]]}]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"py-14 sm:py-20 flex-grow bg-gray-50","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["If you are asking how much does a loft conversion cost in the UK, the honest answer is that the final price depends on far more than the size of the loft. The type of conversion, roof structure, access, staircase, plumbing, electrics, insulation, windows and level of finish all make a difference. As a rough guide, many UK homeowners may budget between £30,000 and £100,000 or more, although every project is different. A straightforward conversion in an accessible roof may cost less than a complex design requiring major structural alterations. For accurate pricing, request a free, no-obligation quote."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Typical UK loft conversion costs by type"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["The figures below are broad guide prices rather than fixed quotations. They can vary by region, specification, access and the condition of the existing house. Labour and material costs can vary between areas. Every project is different, so these figures should be treated as a starting point only; request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Roof light conversion: as a rough guide, typically £30,000–£45,000. This can be a less disruptive option because the existing roof shape is largely retained. It may suit a loft that already has enough headroom and floor space, with roof windows added for light."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Rear dormer conversion: as a rough guide, typically £45,000–£75,000. A dormer can extend the usable floor area and create more headroom, but it involves additional structural work, external cladding or roofing, windows and internal finishing."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Hip-to-gable conversion: as a rough guide, typically £55,000–£85,000. This changes a sloping side roof into a vertical wall and can create more internal width. It is often combined with a rear dormer, which can increase the overall cost."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Mansard conversion: as a rough guide, typically £65,000–£100,000 or more. This is a substantial alteration that can create a large room but involves significant structural and external work. Planning requirements and design complexity may also be greater."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["More complex or high-specification projects: £100,000 or above may be possible where the conversion includes extensive structural alterations, a bathroom, bespoke joinery, premium finishes or difficult access."]}]]}]]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"my-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 p-6 sm:p-8 border border-[#C8A97E]/30","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-2","children":"Thinking about your own project?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["BMB Renovation covers Watford, Bushey, Rickmansworth, St Albans, Hemel Hempstead and beyond — all trades in-house. Call +44 7775 758 717 or send us a message."]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/contact","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] text-white text-sm font-bold hover:bg-[#b39668] transition-colors","children":["Get a Free Quote",["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-arrow-right w-4 h-4","children":[["$","path","1ays0h",{"d":"M5 12h14"}],["$","path","xquz4c",{"d":"m12 5 7 7-7 7"}],"$undefined"]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"What is included in a loft conversion quote?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["A proper quotation should explain what is included rather than giving one unexplained total. The design and preparation stage may include a measured survey, drawings, structural calculations and advice on whether planning permission or other approvals are likely to be needed. Some contractors include these items in the main price, while others list them separately, so it is important to check before comparing quotes."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Planning, design and approvals"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Some loft conversions can be completed under permitted development rights, while others require a planning application. This depends on factors such as the proposed size, roof shape, position of extensions and the property’s location. A property in a conservation area, or one affected by local restrictions, may need additional consideration. Building regulations approval is separate from planning permission and addresses the technical requirements for the work. Ask your designer or contractor to identify which applications, drawings and inspections are included, and whether application fees are extra."]}],["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-8 mb-3","children":"Structural work and access"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Structural work is often one of the largest parts of the budget. A loft floor may need strengthening, new steel beams may be required, and the roof structure may need altering to create a clear room. The design of the staircase affects both cost and the layout of the floor below. A staircase may require changes to ceilings, flooring, doors, lighting or storage. Scaffolding, skips, temporary protection and site access should also be identified in the quote, as these costs can otherwise appear as surprises later."]}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"my-5 space-y-2.5","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Insulation, plasterboard and fire-resistant construction where required for the design."]}]]}],["$","li","1",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Roof windows, dormer windows, external doors or larger glazing, including flashings and making good."]}]]}],["$","li","2",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Electrical installation, lighting, sockets, smoke or heat detection and any upgrades needed to the existing system."]}]]}],["$","li","3",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Heating and plumbing, particularly if you want an en-suite bathroom or a radiator in the new room."]}]]}],["$","li","4",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Plastering, painting, flooring, skirting, doors, ironmongery and built-in storage."]}]]}],["$","li","5",{"className":"flex gap-3 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] flex-shrink-0"}],["$","span",null,{"children":["Waste removal, scaffolding, protection of existing areas and final cleaning."]}]]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"Common extras that can increase the final cost"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["The difference between an initial estimate and a final account can come from choices made after the project has started. An en-suite bathroom adds plumbing, drainage, ventilation, waterproofing, sanitaryware, tiling and electrical work. Moving a soil pipe or connecting new drainage can be more involved than expected. Premium roof windows, larger dormers, bespoke wardrobes, engineered timber flooring and high-end bathroom fittings can also raise the specification."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["The condition of the existing roof and house matters too. Repairs to old coverings, chimney alterations, hidden timber decay, asbestos-containing materials, inadequate drainage or outdated electrics may not be visible during an initial inspection. Difficult access can increase labour, delivery and scaffolding costs. If the project is in a terraced or closely built-up property, protecting neighbouring buildings and managing deliveries may require additional planning. It is sensible to discuss an appropriate contingency for unforeseen work based on the property and survey findings."]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 tracking-tight mt-12 mb-4","children":"How to compare loft conversion quotes"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Do not choose a contractor on the headline figure alone. Check whether each quote covers design work, structural calculations, approvals, scaffolding, waste removal, insulation, windows, electrics, plumbing, decorating and flooring. Confirm the specification of doors, sanitaryware, sockets, light fittings and finishes, as allowances can make two apparently similar quotes very different. Also ask how variations will be priced if you change the design or if hidden defects are found."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["A local renovation team can help you assess the whole project rather than treating the loft as an isolated room. BMB Renovation, based at 157 Judge Street, Watford WD24 5AN, carries out loft conversions alongside house renovations, bathroom fitting and renovation, carpentry, flooring, tiling, painting and decorating. Plumbing, tiling, electrical and cabinet installation work is handled in-house. Homeowners in Watford, Bushey, Rickmansworth, St Albans, Hemel Hempstead, Borehamwood, Harrow, Croxley Green, Luton and Bedford can review the wider ",["$","$L4","0",{"href":"/services","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"renovation services"}]," or request a ",["$","$L4","1",{"href":"/contact","className":"text-[#C8A97E] font-medium underline decoration-[#C8A97E]/40 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-[#C8A97E] transition-colors","children":"free, no-obligation quote"}],"."]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed my-5","children":["Before committing, obtain a survey or feasibility assessment, decide what the room needs to achieve and set a realistic specification. A bedroom with roof windows will have a different budget from a dormer with an en-suite and fitted storage. The clearest route to an accurate figure is a site visit followed by a written, itemised quotation that explains assumptions, exclusions and possible extra costs."]}],["$","aside",null,{"className":"my-10 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900 p-6 sm:p-8 border border-[#C8A97E]/30","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"font-display text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight mb-2","children":"Get a Free, No-Obligation Quote"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-white/70 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed mb-5","children":["BMB Renovation handles kitchens, bathrooms and full home renovations across Watford, Hertfordshire, North London & Bedfordshire — all trades in-house. Tell us about your project today."]}],["$","$L4",null,{"href":"/contact","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-[#C8A97E] text-white text-sm font-bold hover:bg-[#b3966